#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "List or filter backends {#list-or-filter-backends}"
msgstr "Listar ou filtrar backends {#list-or-filter-backends}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"available\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"available\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "List backends available to you {#list-backends-available-to-you}"
msgstr ""
"Listar os backends disponíveis para você {#list-backends-available-to-you}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can use either Qiskit or IBM Quantum Platform to view a list of backends"
" available to you, or to search for a particular backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Você pode usar o Qiskit ou o IBM Quantum Platform para visualizar uma lista "
"de backends disponíveis ou buscar um backend específico.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"QPU names\">\n"
"QPUs hosted on IBM Cloud&reg; have names that begin with `ibm_*`. All QPUs are given a city name - for example, `ibm_kingston`. This name does not indicate where the actual QPU is hosted.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Nomes de QPUs\">\n"
"QPUs hospedadas no IBM Cloud&reg; têm nomes que começam com `ibm_*`. Todas as QPUs recebem o nome de uma cidade — por exemplo, `ibm_kingston`. Esse nome não indica onde a QPU real está hospedada.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit-available\" label=\"View backends with Qiskit\">\n"
"        Use the [`QiskitRuntimeService.backends()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#backends) method, as shown in the next code block. This method returns a list of [`IBMBackend`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/ibm-backend) instances.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit-available\" label=\"View backends with Qiskit\">\n"
"        Use the [`QiskitRuntimeService.backends()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#backends) method, as shown in the next code block. This method returns a list of [`IBMBackend`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/ibm-backend) instances.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        To run the following code, be sure you have already authenticated to"
" the service. See [Set up your IBM Cloud account](/guides/cloud-setup) for "
"more details.\n"
msgstr ""
"        To run the following code, be sure you have already authenticated to"
" the service. See [Set up your IBM Cloud account](/guides/cloud-setup) for "
"more details.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        To search for a specific backend, use the "
"[`QiskitRuntimeService.backend()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#backend) method (note that this is "
"singular: *backend*), which takes the name of the backend as the input "
"parameter and returns an "
"[`IBMBackend`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/ibm-"
"backend) instance representing that particular backend:\n"
msgstr ""
"        To search for a specific backend, use the "
"[`QiskitRuntimeService.backend()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#backend) method (note that this is "
"singular: *backend*), which takes the name of the backend as the input "
"parameter and returns an "
"[`IBMBackend`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/ibm-"
"backend) instance representing that particular backend:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP-available\" label=\"View backends on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        To view the backends you have access to, navigate to the list of backends on the [Compute resources page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) (note that your selected region might impact the QPUs listed). Click the filter icon and choose either \"All my instances\" or a specific instance name to see the available QPUs.\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP-available\" label=\"View backends on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        Para visualizar os backends aos quais você tem acesso, navegue até a lista de backends na [página Recursos de computação](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) (note que sua região selecionada pode afetar as QPUs listadas). Clique no ícone de filtro e escolha \"All my instances\" ou um nome de instância específico para ver as QPUs disponíveis.\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   If you are logged in to a specific instance or region, or if you initialized the service with a specific instance or region by using `QiskitRuntimeService()`, only the backends available to you on that instance or region are returned.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"   Se você estiver conectado a uma instância ou região específica, ou se tiver inicializado o serviço com uma instância ou região específica usando `QiskitRuntimeService()`, apenas os backends disponíveis para você nessa instância ou região serão retornados.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Filter backends {#filter-backends}"
msgstr "Filtrar backends {#filter-backends}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit-filter\" label=\"Filter by properties with Qiskit\">\n"
"        You can filter the available backends by their [configuration](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/models-backend-configuration) or [status](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/models-backend-status). For more general filters, set the `filters` argument to a function that accepts a backend object and returns `True` if it meets your criteria. Refer to the [API documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#backends) for more details.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"Qiskit-filter\" label=\"Filter by properties with Qiskit\">\n"
"        Você pode filtrar os backends disponíveis pela sua [configuração](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/models-backend-configuration) ou [status](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/models-backend-status). Para filtros mais gerais, defina o argumento `filters` como uma função que aceita um objeto de backend e retorna `True` se ele atender aos seus critérios. Consulte a [documentação da API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#backends) para mais detalhes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        The following code returns only backends that fit these criteria and"
" are available to you _on your currently selected instance_:\n"
msgstr ""
"        O código a seguir retorna apenas os backends que atendem a estes "
"critérios e estão disponíveis para você _na sua instância atualmente "
"selecionada_:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '        *   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Are real quantum devices (`simulator=False`)\n"
msgstr "São dispositivos quânticos reais (`simulator=False`)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '        *   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Are currently operational (`operational=True`)\n"
msgstr "Estão atualmente operacionais (`operational=True`)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '        *   '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Have at least a hundred qubits (`min_num_qubits=100`)\n"
msgstr "Têm pelo menos cem qubits (`min_num_qubits=100`)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"        A similar method is "
"[`QiskitRuntimeService.least_busy()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#least_busy), which takes the same filters"
" as `backends()` but returns the backend that matches the filters and has "
"the least number of jobs pending in the queue:\n"
msgstr ""
"        Um método similar é "
"[`QiskitRuntimeService.least_busy()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"ibm-runtime/qiskit-runtime-service#least_busy), que aceita os mesmos filtros"
" que `backends()`, mas retorna o backend que corresponde aos filtros e tem o"
" menor número de jobs pendentes na fila:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP-filter\" label=\"Filter by properties on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        To view the backends you have access to, view the table on the [Compute resources page](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers). Click the filter icon to see filter options. You can filter by processor type and status. Note also that you can sort the table by any column by hovering over a column title, and then clicking the arrows that appear.\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"    </TabItem>\n"
"    <TabItem value=\"IQP-filter\" label=\"Filter by properties on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
"        Para visualizar os backends aos quais você tem acesso, veja a tabela na [página Recursos de computação](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers). Clique no ícone de filtro para ver as opções de filtragem. Você pode filtrar por tipo de processador e status. Note também que você pode ordenar a tabela por qualquer coluna passando o cursor sobre o título de uma coluna e clicando nas setas que aparecem.\n"
"    </TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Static backend information {#static-backend-information}"
msgstr "Informações estáticas do backend {#static-backend-information}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Some information about a backend does not change regularly, such as its "
"name, [version](#qpu-versioning), the number of qubits it has, its processor"
" type (the bird family name, which indicates the [topology](#coupling-map) "
"and approximate qubit count), and the types of features it supports. This "
"information is available as attributes of the `backend` object. For a full "
"list of attributes, see the [`IBMBackend` API "
"documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/ibm-"
"backend).  Find more information on versioning in the [QPU versioning](#qpu-"
"versioning) section below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algumas informações sobre um backend não mudam com frequência, como seu "
"nome, [versão](#qpu-versioning), o número de qubits que possui, seu tipo de "
"processador (o nome da família de pássaros, que indica a "
"[topologia](#coupling-map) e a contagem aproximada de qubits), e os tipos de"
" recursos que suporta. Essas informações estão disponíveis como atributos do"
" objeto `backend`. Para uma lista completa de atributos, consulte a "
"[documentação da API IBMBackend](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"ibm-runtime/ibm-backend). Encontre mais informações sobre versionamento na "
"seção [Versionamento de QPU](#qpu-versioning) abaixo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A backend's region (the location of the data center where your data and "
"experiments will be hosted and processed) is listed in its detailed "
"information card on the [Compute "
"resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page on IBM Quantum "
"Platform.\n"
msgstr ""
"A região de um backend (a localização do data center onde seus dados e "
"experimentos serão hospedados e processados) está listada no cartão de "
"informações detalhadas no [Compute "
"resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) no IBM Quantum "
"Platform.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"Qiskit-backend\" label=\"View backend information with Qiskit\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"Qiskit-backend\" label=\"View backend information with Qiskit\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  </TabItem>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"IQP-backend\" label=\"View backend information on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"
msgstr ""
"  </TabItem>\n"
"  <TabItem value=\"IQP-backend\" label=\"View backend information on IBM Quantum Platform\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Navigate to the [Compute "
"resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page to view a table of "
"all QPUs, then click the name of any QPU to open its detailed information "
"card. Find backend information under the Details section of the card.\n"
msgstr ""
"    Navegue até a página [Recursos de "
